---
// Final CTA before the footer. Ref: a straight-on photo of a red shipping
// container's corrugated side, with copy meant to read as if it were painted
// directly onto the container itself. First two passes built the container
// surface in CSS (to avoid an asset dependency) but the user asked for the
// real photo they supplied — trimmed its white margin and upscaled slightly
// (source was 612x251) via sharp, saved to public/cta/container.webp. It's a
// flat-illustration-style render rather than a detailed photo, so the
// upscale stays crisp. A dark gradient sits between the image and the text
// for legibility; no CSS-drawn rivets anymore since the real photo already
// has its own corner castings baked in.
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="container-panel relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl">
      <img src="/cta/container.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-black/45 via-black/15 to-black/50" />

      <div class="relative mx-auto flex max-w-2xl flex-col items-center px-6 py-16 text-center sm:px-12 sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
        <p
          data-reveal
          class="translate-y-8 text-sm font-semibold tracking-[0.25em] text-white/80 uppercase opacity-0 transition-all duration-700 ease-out"
        >
          Get In Touch
        </p>
        <h2 data-reveal class="cta-heading mt-5 translate-y-8 text-2xl leading-tight font-extrabold text-white uppercase opacity-0 transition-all duration-700 ease-out sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl">
          Let Us Take the Burden of Your Cargo
        </h2>
        <p
          data-reveal
          class="mt-5 max-w-xl translate-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/90 opacity-0 [text-shadow:0_2px_6px_rgba(0,0,0,0.4)] transition-all delay-150 duration-700 ease-out sm:text-base"
        >
          Talk to our team and get a tailored freight solution built around your cargo, wherever it needs to go.
        </p>

        <a
          href="/quote"
          data-reveal
          class="cta-button group mt-8 inline-flex translate-y-8 items-center gap-2 rounded-full px-7 py-3.5 text-sm font-bold text-brand-red opacity-0 transition-all delay-300 duration-700 ease-out hover:-translate-y-0.5 sm:text-base"
        >
          Get a Quote
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4 transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">
            <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .container-panel {
    box-shadow:
      0 30px 60px -20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35),
      0 10px 24px -10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  }

  .cta-heading {
    /* debossed/stamped-metal lettering: a soft light catch on the upper edge
       plus a deeper drop shadow below, rather than a single flat shadow */
    text-shadow:
      0 -1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25),
      0 3px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25),
      0 8px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .cta-button {
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #ffffff, #f3f4f6);
    box-shadow:
      0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6) inset,
      0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }

  .cta-button:hover {
    box-shadow:
      0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6) inset,
      0 14px 36px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  }
</style>
